[["Spoken to the Psyche Core Tertiary after commenting on «Short-term prototypes: Clojure now?». STT, 2026-10-14." "I've commented on the Clojure prototypes and I want to design a standard way to translate an ethos specification to essentially a Clojure type, I guess, that can be represented in EDN instead of datom. For both Clojure and EDN let's work out a context module for this: how we translate an ethos and datom syntax into Clojure and EDN."] ["Same speech, on proposals of code. STT, 2026-10-14." "I don't want proposals to code. If you want to propose code to me, I want you to propose an approach or a pattern, or some wrapping code that will become standard, like a standard entry point or a standard pattern."] ["Comment on P3's example, the added line :worker {:model \"gpt-5.6-terra\" ...}. 2026-10-14." "Of all the models of OpenAI, the one we don't use anymore is Terra so that's a really bad example. Until Terra 6 comes out we're not touching Terra."]]
